      "id": "claim_8a07020c5d4c4166b97fd68e71e6591d",
      "statement": "main() wires the shell: single-instance (refocus existing window), window-state (size/position/maximized), dialog, updater, a custom slr-os plugin injecting window.__SLR_OS__ with Node-style platform/arch names, a deny-all on_permission_request, .manage() of update::State, close::Guard and Mutex<Session>, and the slr-file scheme registered as an asynchronous protocol handler serving each request on a spawned thread; the run() closure intercepts ExitRequested{code:None} and CloseRequested through close::intercept and calls localruntime::stop_all() on RunEvent::Exit so managed llama.cpp servers are killed.",
