      "statement": "llm_call pins the call to the configured origin: it refuses to send the key unless the named URL's scheme matches and its origin equals the config baseUrl's origin, follows no redirects (NO_REDIRECT client) since a 3xx would carry the Authorization header to an unchecked origin, and for managed catalogId targets redirects the call to the shell-run llama.cpp server's 127.0.0.1 endpoint with its per-session key, restricted to /v1/* and /health paths via the proxy-free LOOPBACK client; calls run under Flight id llm:<requestId> with a 10-minute timeout.",
