    {
      "id": "claim_a959133aa2284871826faf94adc3d8bb",
      "statement": "webfetch.rs guards web:fetch against SSRF from LLM-supplied URLs: validate_fetch_url re-runs on every hop (http/https only, no embedded credentials, blocked literal IP ranges and localhost/.local/.internal/.localhost hostnames refused — blocked v4 includes 0/8, 10/8, 127/8, 100.64/10, 169.254/16, 172.16/12, 192.168/16 and ≥224; blocked v6 covers loopback, unspecified, v4-mapped, fe80, fc/fd, ff), check_public_host refuses domains with any non-public address, and the PublicOnly reqwest DNS resolver re-runs the same rule for the actual connection, closing the DNS-rebinding window; redirects are followed manually with re-validation up to 5 hops, with a 20-second timeout, a 2 MB body cap (truncated flag), and a textual-content-type gate.",
      "evidence": [
