      "statement": "close.rs implements the unsaved-changes guard as a Guard of four atomics (dirty, asking, saving, allow) managed in main(): the run closure intercepts user-initiated ExitRequested{code:None} and WindowEvent::CloseRequested; when dirty it shows the native Save / Don't Save / Cancel dialog once (asking dedupes), Save emits app:requestSave and only app_save_complete(ok=true) from that guard-requested save (not any ordinary saveComplete) exits the app via app.exit(0), Don't Save latches allow so every later close passes, and Cancel keeps the window open; the renderer's useCloseGuard pushes both stores' combined dirty state via app:setDirty.",
